  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nThe stronger offshore flow will continue into Friday with ECMWF\nensemble output still showing the strongest offshore winds at \nCampo on Friday, then not as strong on Saturday. Winds on Friday \ncould gusts to 45 to 55 mph with easterly Santa Ana winds \nextending to near the coast in San Diego County.\n\nHigh temperatures will continue to warm on Friday, then cool a few\nto around 5 degrees on Saturday. High temperatures on Friday for\nthe beaches will be in the mid 80s to lower 90s. Elsewhere for the\ncoast and valleys, high temperatures will range from the upper 70s\nto mid 80s for the far inland valleys to the upper 80s to mid 90s\nfor inland coastal areas into the far western valleys. Moderate \nto locally Major HeatRisk is expected for coastal areas into the \nwestern valleys for Friday, then mostly Moderate HeatRisk just for\ncoastal areas on Saturday. \n\nFor Sunday and Monday, cooling will spread inland into the coast\nand valleys while the mountains and deserts warm. High\ntemperatures for next Monday will be mostly a few to around 5\ndegrees above average to 5 to 10 degrees above average for San\nDiego County coastal areas. On Monday, high temperatures will\nrange from the mid 70s to lower 80s near the coast to the 80s for\nthe Inland Empire with the lower deserts in the lower 90s.\n\nThat cutoff low pressure system could transport some tropical \nnorthward into the area by the weekend into early next week. While\nprecipitation chances will remain low and be mainly for the lower\ndeserts eastward into Arizona, it should put a floor on any \ndecrease in humidity with the offshore flow with lowest humidity \nfor inland coastal areas into the valleys of 20 to 30 percent on \nThursday and Friday and 25 to 35 percent on Saturday.",
